{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Come up to Me on the mountain.</b> To the top of the mountain — for even after Moses drew nearer than the rest who went up with him, as it says: וְנִגַּשׁ מֹשֶׁה לְבַדּוֹ (Exodus 24:2), he still did not ascend to the top of the mountain. And at that station the elders attained the great vision. He told Moses to ascend to the top of the mountain, for there was the appearance of the glory of YHWH, as it says: וּמַרְאֵה כְּבוֹד ה' כְּאֵשׁ אֹכֶלֶת בְּרֹאשׁ הָהָר, and so too at the giving of the Torah it says: אֶל רֹאשׁ הָהָר וַיִּקְרָא ה' לְמֹשֶׁה אֶל רֹאשׁ הָהָר (Exodus 19:20)." "<b>And be there.</b> Remain there for some extended time, as in: וַיִּהְיוּ שָׁם כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוַּנִי ה' (Deuteronomy 10:5)." "<b>And the Torah.</b> The speculative part of it." "<b>And the commandment.</b> That is the practical part of it." "<b>Which I have written.</b> For had they not sinned with the calf, the entire Torah would have been given sealed from the hand of the Creator, blessed be He, like the tablets — as He testified, saying (Deuteronomy 33:2): וְאָתָה מֵרִבְבוֹת קֹדֶשׁ, מִימִינוֹ אֵשׁ דָּת לָמוֹ וְכוּ'. But ever since they sinned with the calf they were not worthy of this; instead Moses wrote it at His command, as it says afterward (Exodus 34:27): כְּתָב־לְךָ אֶת־הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה. And Moses our Master brought the tablets only in order to break them before their eyes, to break their adulterous heart, so that they would return in repentance." "<b>To teach them.</b> I give them to you so that you may teach them. For even though all is in writing — as they said, of blessed memory (Ta'anit 9a): מִי אִיכָּא מִידִי בִּנְבִיאֵי וּכְתוּבֵי דְּלָא רְמָזָהּ מֹשֶׁ בְּאוֹרַיְיתָא, and as some of them said, of blessed memory (Gittin 60b): רֹב בִּכְתָב וּמִעוּט בְּעַל פֶּה — the allusions contained in it, in speculation and in practice, will not be understood by the majority of Israel except through a righteous teacher. And in this, the statement of some of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, is also justified, where they said (ibid.): רֹב בְּעַל פֶּה וּמִעוּט בִּכְתָב."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:15.949928306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}